{{Top}}
{{Quote|It is something approaching the sacred, really. A vital part of our identity.''"<br />"''Mmmm.''"<br />"''For the Twi'leks, the caressing of the lekku is an act that is beyond mere sensuality.|[[Kaasha Bateen]] and [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]]|<ref name="Last Shot">''[[Last Shot]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Two_kinds_of_lekku.jpg|thumb|250px|Both the Twi'leks (left) and the Togruta (right) had lekku.]]
'''Lekku''' (singular '''lek'''), also referred to as '''head-tails''' or '''brain-tails''', were long, fleshy appendages that protruded from the head of all [[Twi'lek]]s, [[Togruta]], [[Tosarvi]], [[Waluna]]s, and [[Gender|male]] [[Ozrelanso]]. The Togruta sported three of them, while the other [[species]] had two (occasionally four, in the case of Twi'leks).

==In Twi'leks==
{{Quote|It's bitten off his ''lekku'', Winloss. He'll be dead in an hour.|[[Nokk]], on the Twi'lek Squoxx|<ref name="DAAnnual 2">[[Doctor Aphra Annual 2|''Doctor Aphra Annual'' 2]]</ref>}}
In [[Twi'lek]]s, lekku were shapely prehensile tentacles that grew from the crown of their skulls. While Twi'leks normally had two lekku,<ref name="AbEverything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> certain individuals like [[Orn Free Taa]] had four of them.<ref name="RotS">{{Film|III}}</ref> Super-sensitive lekku could be used for grabbing and holding objects. Those organs were very sensitive to touch, and a damaged lek could cause severe harm to a Twi'lek;<ref name="AbEverything" /> [[Squoxx]] [[Death|died]] within an [[Standard hour|hour]] after one of his lekku was bitten off.<ref name="DAAnnual 2" /> Lekku loss did not always kill Twi'leks, however: the [[Jedi Master]] [[Loden Greatstorm]] lived for some time after his lekku were [[Dismemberment|cut off]] while he was in the captivity of the [[Nihil]]. If not for his later death in [[Battle of Grizal|battle]], Greatstorm would have been fitted with prosthetic replacements.<ref name="Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref>

In addition to their spoken [[language]], [[Twi'leki|Ryl]]<ref name="LOTS">''[[Lords of the Sith]]''</ref>, the Twi'leks could also communicate through subtle lekku gestures.<ref name="DB Ryloth">{{Databank|ryloth|Ryloth}}</ref> For example, the right lek tip raised meant "hello," the left lek tip dipped meant "goodbye," both lekku tips crossed over twice meant "love you," and both lekku tips jabbed into the speaker's back meant "may [[spice]] salt your wounds!" Despite the high sensitivity of those organs,<ref name="AbEverything" /> Tw'lek Jedi [[Matthea Cathley]] had a habit of smoothing over her Lekku with her hands if her mind was racing through thoughts. Her friend [[Tey Sirrek]] also claimed her lekku twitched whenever she lied, which she disputed. She also demonstrated the ability to shake her lekku.<ref name="Path of Vengeance">''[[The High Republic: Path of Vengeance]]''</ref> Some Twi'leks like [[Cham Syndulla]] [[tattoo]]ed their lekku.<ref name="Homecoming Concept">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/homecoming-concept-art-gallery|text="Homecoming" Concept Art Gallery}}</ref> Some wore them simply hanging down their back<ref name="TD">{{TCW|The Deserter}}</ref> or falling over the chest<ref name="Obi-Wan & Anakin 2">[[Obi-Wan and Anakin 2|''Obi-Wan and Anakin'' 2]]</ref>, while others like [[Bib Fortuna]] bent them around the neck or shoulders for aesthetic purposes.<ref name="ROTJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref>

==In Togruta==
{{Quote|Farming accident, a long time ago. They can give you prosthetic hands and feet, but they can't do much about your lekku.|[[Vartan]], about Selda's missing lek|<ref name="Ahsoka">[[Ahsoka (novel)|''Ahsoka'']]</ref>}}
[[File:LifeAndDeath.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Lekku grew in size as their wearer matured, starting out only visible around a Togruta's head but eventually reaching past their shoulders and beyond.]]
The name "lekku" was also used to describe the striped head-tails of the [[Togruta]]. That species, however, had three such appendages: two lekku to the front, falling over the chest, and one thicker lek that was centered at the rear base of their skull.<ref name="Epic Battles">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Visual Guide: Epic Battles]]''</ref> As seen on [[Governor]] [[Gupat Roshti]], [[Gender|male]] Togruta's lekku were shorter than those of females.<ref name="Kidnapped">{{TCW|Kidnapped}}</ref> The loss of a lek, as seen on the [[bartender]] [[Selda]], was not a crippling injury, but the appendages did not grow back afterwards.<ref name="Ahsoka" /> A Togruta's [[montral]]s were connected to their lekku. The [[color]] of a Togruta's lekku was determined by their [[DNA]].<ref name="Epic Battles" />

Lekku grew as their wearer matured.<ref name="AotG">''[[Star Wars: Aliens of the Galaxy]]''</ref> As an infant, lekku were only found around the Togruta's head.<ref name="Life and Death">{{TOTJ|Life and Death}}</ref> In adolescence, the lekku extended only slightly past the collarbones, but could reach below the waist by adulthood.<ref name="AotG">''[[Star Wars: Aliens of the Galaxy]]''</ref> The elder Togruta [[Gantika]] had lekku that only extended to her stomach.<ref name="Life and Death" />

==In Ozrelanso==
In male [[Ozrelanso]], lekku were tentacles that grew on the sides of their skulls.<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Lekku first appeared in the film [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']], along with the Twi'lek species.<ref name="ROTJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> In ''[[The High Republic: Into the Dark]]'', Togruta [[Jedi]] Master [[Jora Malli]]'s lekku are misidentified as her [[montral]]s when the appendages are described as streaming behind her when the [[airspeeder]] she is riding goes into a dive.<ref name="ItD">''[[The High Republic: Into the Dark]]''</ref> [[Ahsoka Tano]]'s lekku lost length between her animated<ref name="Fire">{{Rebels|Fire Across the Galaxy}}</ref> by [[4 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> and live action depictions.<ref name="Chapter 13">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 13: The Jedi}}</ref> For ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]'', her lekku were slightly extended.<ref name="Part One">{{Ahsoka|Part One: Master and Apprentice}}</ref>

